摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Harness agent plugin that acts as a sentinel between the AI agent and MCP servers — polling long-running tasks so token-costly status loops never enter the LLM inference path","id":"gh:1311702182","install_available":false,"language":"TypeScript","name":"mcp-sentinel","slug":"GCS-ZHN/mcp-sentinel","topics":["dsh-plugin","opencode-plugin"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Harness agent plugin that acts as a sentinel between the AI agent and MCP servers — polling long-run"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"ning tasks so token-costly status loops never enter the LLM inference path"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# mcp-sentinel"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"A **sentinel** between an AI agent and MCP servers — polling long-running tasks on the agent's behal"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"f so that token-costly status loops never enter the LLM inference path."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"This is a **monorepo**: a harness-agnostic core (`@gcszhn/mcp-sentinel-core`) plus one thin plugin p"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"ackage per agent host."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"## Design principle"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"**Zero MCP re-configuration.** The sentinel never asks the user to configure MCP\nservers of its own."},{"id":"p6s2","text":" Installing the plugin is the whole setup — it discovers and\nreuses the MCP servers the harness alre"},{"id":"p6s3","text":"ady has, in whichever way that harness\nexposes them:"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"- **From the host's MCP config** — OpenCode. The plugin reads\n`client.config.get().mcp` and hands th"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"e resolved servers to the core, which\nowns the connection lifecycle. No extra MCP setup.\n- **Through"},{"id":"p7s3","text":" the harness SDK** — DeepSeek Harness. The plugin calls the\n`mcp__<server>__<tool>` tools already re"},{"id":"p7s4","text":"gistered by\n`@deepseek-ai/dsh-mcp-client` via `ctx.tools.execute`. No extra MCP setup.\n- **As a harn"},{"id":"p7s5","text":"ess-agnostic MCP CLI** — any harness. `mcp-sentinel mcp --harness\n<codex|opencode|custom>` is a plai"},{"id":"p7s6","text":"n stdio MCP server that discovers the MCP\nservers the harness already exposes (`codex mcp list --jso"},{"id":"p7s7","text":"n`, `opencode debug\nconfig`, or a `--mcp-config` file) and skips its own entry. No message\nnotificat"},{"id":"p7s8","text":"ion channel by default — agents collect results with\nattach/status/read, unless they opt into a comm"},{"id":"p7s9","text":"and-based notifier via\n`mcp_sentinel_set_notifier_commands`."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"The agent immediately sees the MCP servers it already configured for that\nharness; there is no senti"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"nel-specific MCP config, mock server, or demo wiring\nto maintain."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## Supported harnesses"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"Install instructions and per-harness details live in each plugin's own README."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"| Harness           | Plugin package                                                                "},{"id":"p11s2","text":"                                               | Docs                                          |"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"| OpenCode          | `@gcszhn/mcp-sentinel-opencode-plugin`                 | README         |\n| De"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"epSeek Harness  | `@gcszhn/mcp-sentinel-deepseek-harness-plugin` | README |\n| Any harness (CLI) | `@"},{"id":"p12s3","text":"gcszhn/mcp-sentinel-cli`                                         | README              |"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"The shared core ships separately as `@gcszhn/mcp-sentinel-core` — see its README."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"## Motivation"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"When an agent submits a long-running job through an MCP tool, it must repeatedly call the server to "},{"id":"p15s2","text":"check progress — each round-trip burns context window tokens."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"**mcp-sentinel** moves the polling loop out of the agent and into the plugin runtime — 2 inference c"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"alls regardless of task duration."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"## Configuration"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"Environment variables for controlling memory usage:"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"| Variable                | Default   | Description                                       |"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"| `SENTINEL_MAX_POLL_LOG` | unlimited | Max poll log entries per task (FIFO trim)         |\n| `SENTI"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"NEL_TASK_TTL_MS`  | unlimited | Auto-cleanup completed tasks after N milliseconds |"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"Both accept positive integers only. Zero, negative, or non-numeric values are treated as unlimited/d"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"ept positive integers only. Zero, negative, or non-numeric values are treated as unlimited/disabled."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"## Tools"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"### `mcp_sentinel_poll`"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"Submit a long-running MCP tool call and poll it at regular intervals until a condition is met. The s"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"entinel polls silently (zero token cost) and notifies you when done."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"| Parameter  | Type   | Default    | Description                                           |"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"| `server`   | string | _required_ | MCP server name (resolved from the host's MCP config) |\n| `tool"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"`     | string | _required_ | Tool name to call on the server                       |\n| `args`     |"},{"id":"p28s3","text":" object | `{}`       | JSON object of arguments for the tool                 |\n| `interval` | number"},{"id":"p28s4","text":" | `5000`     | Poll interval in milliseconds                         |\n| `timeout`  | number | _opt"},{"id":"p28s5","text":"ional_ | Max poll duration in ms (unset = no limit)            |\n| `until`    | object | _required_ "},{"id":"p28s6","text":"| JSON condition object                                 |"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"Returns a sentinel ID immediately. The agent is notified when done (the\ndelivery mechanism is host-s"},{"id":"p29s2","text":" sentinel ID immediately. The agent is notified when done (the\ndelivery mechanism is host-specific)."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"`args` and `until` are **native JSON values** in the tool arguments — not JSON\nstrings. `interval` i"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"s clamped to a minimum of 1000 ms; a positive `timeout` is\nclamped to a minimum of 5000 ms (values b"},{"id":"p30s3","text":"elow the floor are raised)."},{"id":"p31s1","text":"### `mcp_sentinel_status`"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"Check the status of sentinel tasks, list active tasks, or cancel a running task."},{"id":"p33s1","text":"| Parameter | Type                                 | Description                                    "},{"id":"p33s2","text":"arameter | Type                                 | Description                                      |"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"| `action`  | `\"status\"` \\| `\"list\"` \\| `\"cancel\"` | Action to perform                              "},{"id":"p34s2","text":"  |\n| `id`      | string                               | Sentinel ID (required for `status` and `can"},{"id":"p34s3","text":"id`      | string                               | Sentinel ID (required for `status` and `cancel`) |"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"### `mcp_sentinel_attach`"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"Block the agent, waiting for a sentinel task to complete. Sleeps and checks status internally with z"},{"id":"p36s2","text":"ero token cost. If interrupted by harness, the background async notification still fires normally."},{"id":"p37s1","text":"| Parameter | Type   | Default    | Description                                     |"},{"id":"p38s1","text":"| `id`      | string | _required_ | Sentinel ID to wait for                         |\n| `timeout` | "},{"id":"p38s2","text":"number | _optional_ | Max wait time in ms (unset = wait indefinitely) |"},{"id":"p39s1","text":"### `mcp_sentinel_read`"},{"id":"p40s1","text":"Read raw poll outputs from a sentinel task. Useful for debugging when a condition isn't matching — i"},{"id":"p40s2","text":"nspect actual MCP responses. Supports range-based pagination via `offset`."},{"id":"p41s1","text":"| Parameter | Type   | Default    | Description                             |"},{"id":"p42s1","text":"| `id`      | string | _required_ | Sentinel ID to read outputs from        |\n| `offset`  | number |"},{"id":"p42s2","text":" `end-N`    | 0-based start index (default: from end) |\n| `limit`   | number | `5`        | Max numb"},{"id":"p42s3","text":"er of outputs to return         |"},{"id":"p43s1","text":"## Architecture"},{"id":"p44s1","text":"The project is a **monorepo** where each layer ships as its own npm package. The\ncore knows nothing "},{"id":"p44s2","text":"about any host; every harness is a thin, self-contained\npackage layered on top of it."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
